From eb11fff487c0bde6ad820b3afc5a1cb9b00dca31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:55:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban pacing: a burn rate no longer holds card
 starts (pace_starts, default false)

The governor is about worker slots; the token rate is the token throttle's
job. 2026-11-17: with the Claude and Codex pools both paced, every host was
cut to one run per provider (3 of 18 slots busy, 130 cards waiting) while
the pools still held over two account-weeks.

admit_limit now limits only a held pool (no account under its reserve)
unless kanban.llm_pacing.pace_starts is true, which keeps the earlier
proportional limit. The pace is still read, judged and stored, so the
held reroute, notices and the throughput panel's runway are unchanged.

Tests that pin the proportional limit opt in explicitly; new tests cover
the default at the unit and dispatch level.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
